<title>USA: Sacramento, Calif. $225 mln bond too close to call.</title>
<headline>Sacramento, Calif. $225 mln bond too close to call.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $225 million Sacramento City Unified School District bond measure was too close to call Wednesday, election officials said.</p>
<p>Measure E, which would authorize a $225 million, 10-year bond to repair school facilities, had the support of 66.4 percent of voters based on unofficial election results. But some absentee and provisional ballots must still be counted.</p>
<p>The measure will require two-thirds support to pass.</p>
<p>If it passes, the school district said it plans to seek matching state funds.</p>
